{"ref":"BDB, אָנַק","hw":"אָנַק","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אָנַק</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. cry, groan (</strong>Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲנַק</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܶܢܰܩ</span> <strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>Qal</strong>  Impf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יֶאֱנֹק</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:52\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.52\">Je 51:52</a>; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֱנֹק</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 26:15\" href=\"/Ezekiel.26.15\">Ez 26:15</a>, both of groaning of wounded <span dir=\"rtl\">(חָלָל)</span>.<br><strong>Niph.</strong>  <em>id.</em>, in mourning, lamentation; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵאָנֵק</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.17\">Ez 24:17</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">עָשָׂה אֵבֶל</span>); Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶאֱנָקִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 9:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.9.4\">9:4</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶאֱנָחִים</span>) sq. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span>.","next":"BDB, אֲנָקָה","prev":"BDB, אֲנָפָה"}